{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":242551,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ff71457a-5be3-4b4f-ab5a-22d96999063b","total_cost_usd":1.0760945,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56606,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"output_tokens":18542,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56606,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18542,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56606},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":37881,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.037991,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18542,"cacheReadInputTokens":16967,"cacheCreationInputTokens":56606,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0381035,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"playtester\",\n  \"verdict\": \"targets_missed\",\n  \"summary\": \"Flown, this configuration has no aerobraking ladder at all — the staged ballistic coefficient of 8.9 kg/m2 means a single plunge is the cheapest descent from every band at every load, shallow unstaged passes peak at 7x the heat bar, and a full hold burns 151-188% of a 100% shield plate; fix the frontal area first, then replace the U-shaped ablation curve with the fallback §4.5 already names.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"aerobraking_ladder_absent\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"The intended descent is a sequence of committed braking passes, with staging as the final commit; the baseline's own drag ladder puts the staged ship at 98.5 kg/m2 ballistic coefficient and predicts 'a 2-4 pass descent falls straight out of this ladder before any tuning'.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Flown, staged ballistic coefficient is 8.9 kg/m2 and unstaged is 28.6 kg/m2 — both below the ~50 floor at which the atmosphere stops the ship rather than braking it. Every multi-pass trajectory the sim could find brakes at 77-88 m inside a 90 m atmosphere, i.e. it skims the very top uselessly, and peak heat goes UP with pass count instead of down (suborbital full hold: 187 at 1 pass, 203 at 2, 205 at 10, 207 at 13). There is no intermediate depth available: a pass deep enough to brake is deep enough to end the flight. The exploration grid satisfies aerobraking_exists in 74.7% of 324 worlds, so the ladder is reachable — this configuration just is not on it.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ablation_optimum_is_always_one_pass\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"ablation.optimal_pass_count is 3 in every band, and the emitted cost_curve minimises at index 3 (21.95 suborbital, 25.92 low, 34.29 high), with a single plunge costing 1.88x the optimum and eight feathered passes 1.60x.\",\n      \"measured\": \"cheapest_pass_count is 1 in all nine band x load descents. Measured ablation rises monotonically with pass count wherever more than one count is reachable: low band empty 44.1 / 64.6 / 85.7% for 1 / 2 / 3 passes; high band full hold 188.2 / 232.3 / 252.3 / 262.0 / 264.8% for 1-5. The single-pass figure reproduces the params' own curve exactly (41.2 measured vs 41.18 authored, suborbital empty), so the cost formula was implemented as authored — what fails is that real trajectories never deliver the low-heat multi-pass option the formula assumes. Across the exploration grid, optimum_in_window is satisfied in 3.1% of configurations (10 of 324) and in 0 of the 12 top-scoring worlds. This is §4.5 risk 1 occurring, not a missed value: the U-curve does not survive contact with the trajectories, and the GDD's named fallback (flat per-pass cost plus a hard cap on passes, with survivability rather than cost forbidding the plunge) is the move.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unstaged_pass_not_survivable\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"Shallow unstaged passes are survivable because cargo damage only begins at 100% heat; coarse braking happens before staging, while thrust remains to reshape the orbit between passes. unstaged_heat_multiplier = 3.2 is derived from the 317/98.5 ballistic-coefficient ratio.\",\n      \"measured\": \"A shallow unstaged braking pass peaks at 696 heat from the suborbital band and 734 from the low band, against a 100 bar — roughly 7x, not 3.2x. The pre-stage phase of the intended descent profile does not exist: the player cannot touch the atmosphere before staging. That removes the timing decision the section names as the skill ('the skill is when'), leaving staging as a mandatory prerequisite rather than a commit. The controlling quantity is the unstaged ballistic coefficient of 28.6 kg/m2, not the multiplier; the grid satisfies unstaged_pass_survivable in 56.5% of worlds.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"full_hold_exceeds_plate_capacity\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"plate_capacity_pct is 100 at base, 140 at heat_shield tier 1 and 190 at tier 2; a depleted plate behaves as unshielded and burns cargo slot by slot.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The cheapest available full-hold descent costs 151.1% (suborbital), 161.3% (low) and 188.2% (high) of plate; plate_survives is false in all three. A half hold from the high band already costs 115.8% and also fails. So at base shield a full hold cannot be returned from any band including the starting one, and at maximum shield (190) the high-band full hold clears by 1.8 points with zero margin for a second attempt or any attitude error. Empty returns are fine: 41.2 / 44.1 / 51.6%.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"heat_bar_saturates_on_every_laden_return\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"reentry.heat_capacity is 100 and cargo damage begins at 100% heat, one slot every 3 s, with fragile pieces taking double — so cargo damage is the price of a hot reentry, not the default outcome. GDD 2.3.6 lists the heat shield upgrade as buying 'heat capacity & plate thickness'.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Peak heat with any cargo aboard: half hold 149 / 153 / 164 and full hold 187 / 192 / 206 across suborbital / low / high. Every laden return from every band pins the bar for a sustained stretch, so cargo damage is guaranteed rather than earned. Worse, no upgrade in the set moves it: both heat_shield tiers change plate_capacity_pct only, and reentry.heat_capacity stays 100 forever, so this is the one reentry cost the player cannot buy margin against.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cargo_mass_triples_the_ship\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.5\",\n      \"claim\": \"A full hold roughly doubles the rocket's mass at starting storage size; the params derive 7.43 kg per slot, a 44.6 kg hold and a 1.99x ratio against dry_mass_kg 45.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The sim flew 15.09 kg per slot, a 90.6 kg full hold and a 3.01x mass ratio. 15.09 is the balancer's own low-band figure (15.3 kg/slot), not its suborbital one, so the flown catalog mix is a band up from the one the doubling claim was authored against. This is upstream of most of the other findings: touchdown speed, ablation and peak heat were all authored at roughly half the mass actually flown, which is why they miss in the same direction.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"full_hold_landing_is_hard\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"landing.descent_speed_full_hold_ms is 4.6, sitting 0.4 m/s under the 5.0 soft-landing line, with descent speed growing as the square root of mass.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Touchdown is 3.28 m/s empty, 4.68 at half hold and 5.78 at full hold — over the soft line in every band, so soft_landing is false for all three full-hold descents. The sqrt-of-mass relation itself holds exactly (3.28 / 4.68 / 5.78 tracks sqrt of 45 / 90.3 / 135.6 kg to within 1%), so the rule is right and only the anchor mass is wrong. Grid: full_hold_lands_soft is satisfied in 16.7% of worlds, so it is reachable but not common.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"band_curve_is_weak_mass_curve_is_strong\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.7\",\n      \"claim\": \"Each altitude band up is disproportionately hotter to return from, so the value curve and the risk curve rise together.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Single-pass ablation for an empty ship is 41.2 / 44.1 / 51.6% across suborbital / low / high — a 1.25x spread top to bottom, matching the Researcher's predicted 1.27 and nothing like 'disproportionate'. The same-band mass swing is 3.7x (suborbital empty 41.2 to full hold 151.1). Grid: difficulty_rises_with_band is satisfied in only 52.5% of worlds, i.e. roughly a coin flip. The curve does rise, but it is carried entirely by cargo mass, which is exactly the lever §4.5 risk 2 names; altitude alone will not hold it, and the second lever there (band-gated ablation rates, already present as fixed_toll_per_pass_pct_by_band 4.0 / 4.6 / 5.8) is currently too small to matter against a 151-point mass effect.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"low_band_gate_leaks\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.7\",\n      \"claim\": \"Base delta-v of 296.1 m/s is deliberately ~4 m/s short of the low-band ascent, so the band gate is the Fuel Tank upgrade rather than pilot skill.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The base ship reached the low band, arriving with 1.06 kg of fuel and a 3.2% margin (suborbital: 3.2 kg, 9.7%). The gate is 3.2% wide, which makes it a skill gate, not a purchase gate. The high band was not reached, which is consistent with it being deferred post-semester and tank-gated — the sim did not fly any upgraded tank, so nothing here says the high band is unreachable after upgrades.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposed_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"baseline.reentry.reference_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": 3.5,\n      \"proposed\": 0.32,\n      \"reason\": \"Restores staged ballistic coefficient to 97 kg/m2 and unstaged to 313 — the Researcher's own ladder — which is the single quantity gating aerobraking_exists and unstaged_pass_survivable, and it is the lever the balancer already flagged rather than a new invention; it costs a ship roughly 0.64 m across, which is an art and camera-scale decision, and the alternative of raising dry_mass_kg back to 500 breaks GDD 2.3.5 far harder now that the flown hold measures 90.6 kg (a 1.18x ratio).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.heat_cost_exponent\",\n      \"current\": 2.2,\n      \"proposed\": 1.0,\n      \"reason\": \"Adopts §4.5 risk 1's own named fallback — flat per-pass cost — because the authored U-curve minimises at 3 on paper and at 1 in every flight, and only 3.1% of 324 grid worlds put the optimum in the 2-4 window at all; the plunge is then barred by the heat bar rather than by price, which is where the anxiety pillar wants it anyway.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.max_passes\",\n      \"current\": null,\n      \"proposed\": 4,\n      \"reason\": \"New field, the second half of the same fallback: with cost flat per pass, a hard cap is what stops feathering (currently up to 26 passes are reachable in the high band at half hold, costing 304.9%), so pass count ends up bracketed by survivability below and the cap above instead of by a cost minimum that does not exist.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"reentry.heat_capacity\",\n      \"current\": 100,\n      \"proposed\": 165,\n      \"reason\": \"Measured peak heat is 149-206 on every laden return, so at 100 the bar is pinned and cargo damage is unavoidable on all of them; 165 leaves empty and half-hold returns clean while full holds still cook, preserving greed_costs_something — and the heat_shield tiers must be wired to raise this field too (GDD 2.3.6 sells 'heat capacity & plate thickness' but both current tiers move plate_capacity_pct only). Re-derive the exact value after the area fix, since all heat figures were flown at the broken ballistic coefficient.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"landing.parachute_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": 48.6,\n      \"proposed\": 77,\n      \"reason\": \"The params never state canopy area — the sim had to solve 48.6 m2 back out of the 4.6 m/s claim — and 77 m2 brings the flown 90.6 kg hold to 4.59 m/s, back under the soft line without touching soft_landing_ms or the parachute upgrade tiers, which still scale on drag coefficient; state it explicitly so the touchdown claim stops being self-referential.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.fuel_capacity_kg\",\n      \"current\": 33,\n      \"proposed\": 31,\n      \"reason\": \"Drops base delta-v from 296 to about 284 m/s so the low band is genuinely behind the Fuel Tank purchase rather than behind a 3.2% margin; the cost is real and should be checked by a human, because it also trims the suborbital reserve from 3.2 kg to roughly 1.2 kg and leaves no room for a wasted burn.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"confidence_notes\": [\n    \"Order matters more than usual here: every heat, ablation and pass-count number in this report was flown at a staged ballistic coefficient of 8.9. If the reference-area change is made, all of it must be re-swept before the heat_capacity and max_passes values are trusted — those two are shaped by the right reasoning but sized against a broken drag ladder.\",\n    \"The heat scale is not a physical unit. The sweep fixed 100 to be the peak of an empty single-pass suborbital descent, so 'peak heat 734' means seven times an empty suborbital plunge, not 734 of anything. Every heat comparison here is a ratio, and the absolute cargo-damage threshold is only meaningful because the params also use 100.\",\n    \"The touchdown finding is a mass finding, not a chute finding. The sim inferred canopy area from the params' own 4.6 m/s claim, so it reproduces 4.6 at 44.6 kg by construction; the 5.78 m/s comes entirely from flying a 90.6 kg hold. If the true suborbital hold is the balancer's 44.6 kg, suborbital full-hold behaviour is the sweep's 'half hold' row — 4.68 m/s, soft, 93% ablation, plate survives — and the landing and plate findings apply from the low band up rather than everywhere. Resolving which catalog mix is correct changes the severity of two findings.\",\n    \"Ignore bands_reachable = 0/324 and fuel_margin_sane = 0/324 as design statements. The exploration grid varies dry mass from 60 to 500 kg while holding thrust, burn rate and the 33 kg tank fixed, so a 500 kg entry has roughly 35 m/s of delta-v and could never reach anything. Those two zeros measure the grid, not the game. The verification sweep's per-band ascent margins are the trustworthy ascent evidence.\",\n    \"The high-band ascent row is self-contradictory — reached = false with 'out of fuel before circularising' alongside fuel_remaining_kg 6.7 and a 20.3% margin. I have treated it as directionally correct (high band not reachable on the base tank) and drawn nothing else from it.\",\n    \"The simulator is a point mass with a perfect pilot: no attitude error, so off_retrograde_penalty = 1.0 is never exercised and every real reentry will run hotter than these figures by the cosine of whatever the player's actual drift is. No debris collisions, no bounce or ground contact model beyond touchdown speed.\",\n    \"Nothing in either sweep touches §2.3.4. Tether shear, tow mass, latch and swing jerk, slot counts and the compactor are entirely unflown here, so the balancer's proof that steady towing cannot shear (165.5 N worst case against a 260 N hold force) stands on algebra alone and phase 3a's tech demo is still the only evidence that will exist for it.\",\n    \"I make no claim about whether any of this feels good. The plasma-to-chute window, whether a 3-pass descent reads as a decision or as arithmetic, and whether a 5.78 m/s touchdown feels like a bruise or a betrayal are Checkpoint 2 and 3 questions and a human has to fly them.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":171465,"ttft_stream_ms":3955,"time_to_request_ms":497,"type":"result","duration_ms":240906,"uuid":"2a666a8f-9279-40d8-bea7-d27ac6cc72dc"}
